problem_statement:
ncsixel_as_rgba fails when sixel image height is greater than 13
`ncsixel_as_rgba` fails when the height of the sixel image exceeds 13 pixels. as far as i can tell, the width is irrelevant -- i tested sixel images over 1000 pixels wide without issue.

the sixel images were mostly generated with `img2sixel`, but i also tested with random sixel images i found online, thinking maybe `img2sixel` was doing something outside of the sixel spec.

but it always fails when the height exceeds 13 pixels.

with `loglevel` set to `trace`, these are the relevant errors:

```
ncsixel_as_rgba:59:expected octothorpe, got 63
ncvisual_from_sixel:803:failed converting sixel to rgba
ncvisual_from_file failed
```

and here is an example sixel image that triggers the bug (22x14)

[alien14.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/15784143/alien14.txt)

thanks!

---

* `export | egrep 'LANG|LC_CTYPE|TERM'`
```
declare -x LANG="en_US.UTF-8"
declare -x TERM="xterm-256color"
declare -x XTERM_LOCALE="en_US.UTF-8"
declare -x XTERM_SHELL="/usr/bin/bash"
declare -x XTERM_VERSION="XTerm(392)"
```
* notcurses version (available from `notcurses-demo i`)
`3.0.9`
* terminal name + version
`XTerm(392)`


ncsixel_as_rgba: incorrect state is set following '-'
oi, there seems to be another bug in `ncsixel_as_rgba` !

```
      }else if(*sx == '$'){
        x = 0;
        state = STATE_WANT_DATA;
      }else if(*sx == '-'){
        x = 0;
        y += 6;
        state = STATE_WANT_HASH;
      }else{
```

setting the state to `STATE_WANT_DATA` after the `-` command fixed it for me

or more concisely, since the state is already `STATE_WANT_DATA` at this point

```
      }else if(*sx == '$'){
        x = 0;
      }else if(*sx == '-'){
        x = 0;
        y += 6;
      }else{
```

the following sixel images will trigger the bug:

[laughing.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/15930780/laughing.txt)
[red40.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/15930781/red40.txt)

been using `notcurses` for a little while now -- really great project :)

patch:
diff --git a/src/lib/sixel.h b/src/lib/sixel.h
index b95a18379..67f13e588 100644
--- a/src/lib/sixel.h
+++ b/src/lib/sixel.h
@@ -161,7 +161,7 @@ uint32_t* ncsixel_as_rgba(const char *sx, unsigned leny, unsigned lenx){
       }else if(*sx == '-'){
         x = 0;
         y += 6;
-        state = STATE_WANT_HASH;
